<title>SOUTH KOREA: Ssangyong cuts petrol price to cheapest in S.Korea.</title>
<headline>Ssangyong cuts petrol price to cheapest in S.Korea.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Ssangyong Oil Refining Co said on Friday it had lowered its retail petrol price to 803 won per litre from 826 won -- the cheapest level offered by the nation's refiners.</p>
<p>The move was taken a day after Yukong Ltd dropped its price to the previous low of 809 won.</p>
<p>Official pump prices offered by Hyundai Oil Refinery Co, Hanwha Energy Co Ltd and LG-Caltex Oil Corp currently stand at 815 won per litre.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
